between our world</i>

456
00:53:58.269 --> 00:53:59.805
<i>and the other world.</i>

457
00:54:03.341 --> 00:54:04.710
<i>In folklore,</i>

458
00:54:05.243 --> 00:54:09.515
<i>rivers, bogs, lakes, and caves</i>

459
00:54:10.315 --> 00:54:12.250
<i>are often seen as places</i>

460
00:54:12.518 --> 00:54:16.154
<i>where fairy folk could enter
the human world.</i>

461
00:54:17.356 --> 00:54:19.592
<i>Or lead humans to theirs.</i>

462
00:54:21.192 --> 00:54:26.264
<i>These sites have been revered
and feared throughout time.</i>

463
00:54:27.332 --> 00:54:28.867
<i>Still to this day,</i>

464
00:54:29.334 --> 00:54:31.837
<i>they are not something
we fully understand.</i>

